# Copy to .env and fill in the three passwords below: compose refuses to start
# without them. Everything after them either has a working default or may be
# left empty, and each says which. `./install.sh` writes this file for you with
# fresh values.
# Generate each password with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Password for the clickmonk Postgres user.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# Password for the clickmonk ClickHouse user.
CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD=
# Signs visitor cookies. At least 32 characters.
CLICKMONK_SECRET=
# IP data downloads (country, ASN, hosting networks and Tor exits), on by
# default. Set to off on a host without internet access: countries then stay
# unknown and the IP checks do not run.
CLICKMONK_IPDATA_UPDATE=on
# Checking that each link domain still publishes its verification TXT record,
# on by default, every five minutes. Off leaves every domain as it was added.
CLICKMONK_DNS_CHECK=on
# Which resolvers to ask, comma separated, each an address and optionally a
# port ([2001:db8::1]:5353 for IPv6). Empty means the host's own.
CLICKMONK_DNS_SERVERS=
# How often the worker looks for clicks and addresses past their retention
# periods. An hour is plenty; shorten it only if you are watching it work. The
# periods themselves are settings on the install, not here:
#   clickmonk settings set --keep-clicks 30 --keep-addresses 7
# Each period is a floor rather than a deadline. Clicks are deleted a whole
# month at a time, so 30 days keeps between 30 and 61 days of them, and the
# same goes for how long an address stays on a click. Running this more often
# does not change that.
CLICKMONK_RETENTION_INTERVAL_MS=3600000
# Where X-Forwarded-For is believed from: comma-separated addresses, ranges
# such as 172.17.0.0/16, or loopback, linklocal and uniquelocal. The default
# names the private and loopback ranges, which is where Caddy is: it is the
# only service in the stack with a published port, and nothing outside can
# reach the redirect to claim an address. Narrow it if you publish the
# redirect yourself, and set your own CDN's ranges in caddy/proxy.d instead
# if one sits in front of Caddy.
# A /0 range is refused.
CLICKMONK_TRUSTED_PROXIES=uniquelocal,loopback
# Optional, and empty unless you set it. The host name the admin API answers
# on. It must not be a link domain: link slugs and admin routes would share one
# namespace, and "domain add" refuses a link domain under this name. A bare
# lower-case host name, with no scheme, no port and no wildcard. The admin
# service refuses to start on anything else and names this variable; the
# redirect logs that it ignored the value and keeps serving links, with the
# certificate check approving verified link domains only, so a typo here costs
# you the admin interface and not your links. Point it at this server, set it
# here, and restart; Caddy obtains a certificate for it on the first HTTPS
# request, and ClickMonk approves that name because you named it here. It needs
# a real name over HTTPS: there is no plain-HTTP way to use the admin API.
# Empty: the admin service answers 503 on every route but its own healthcheck,
# nothing is routed to it, and the CLI is the only way in.
CLICKMONK_ADMIN_HOST=
# The IPv6 range the stack's own Docker network uses. Change it only if it
# collides with a network this host already has.
CLICKMONK_IPV6_SUBNET=fd00:c11c:0::/64
